; The tag-set idiom as CDDL generics — the Cardano ledger's `set<T>` / `nonempty_set<T>` /
; `nonempty_oset<T>` bases, which move from hand-written externs to generated types once the idiom is
; recognized.
;
; The collapse happens at parse time, BEFORE the generic machinery, so a
; `set<a0> = #6.258([* a0]) / [* a0]` choice-bodied generic def stores the already-collapsed Array
; body (a non-collapsed choice-bodied generic def would otherwise hit the finalize-time is_enum
; panic). Each instance resolves to a transparent alias (`pub type SetU64 = Vec<u64>;`), and a field
; typed as an instance serializes through that alias identically to the non-generic equivalent — the
; generic and non-generic paths converge on one resolution.
;
; Instances span uint / text / a struct-typed element so transparent-alias resolution is exercised
; across element kinds; `nonempty_oset` is the third in-the-wild base (conway + dijkstra ledger CDDL)
; proving the mechanism covers N rules, not a hardcoded two. A BYTES element is deliberately omitted:
; a named bytes-element collection alias's wasm wrapper class fails to compile (E0271) regardless of
; this feature — a pre-existing limitation tracked in tests/TESTING_ROADMAP.md; the rust-side bytes
; collapse (incl. per-element StringEncoding preservation) is pinned in-process by
; `optional_tag_set_tests::bytes_element_set_collapses_with_elem_encodings`.
set<a0> = #6.258([* a0]) / [* a0]
nonempty_set<a0> = #6.258([+ a0]) / [+ a0]
nonempty_oset<a0> = #6.258([+ a0]) / [+ a0]
point = [x: uint, y: uint]
holder = [a: set<uint>, b: nonempty_set<text>, c: nonempty_oset<point>]
